# TAN at CRVAL2 = 40 with an explicit LONPOLE = 0 (synthetic, hand-written).
# For a zenithal projection wcslib's default is LONPOLE = 180, so 0 is NOT
# the default here: a reader that ignores an explicit LONPOLE = 0 (treats
# it as "unset") rotates the sky 180 deg about the reference point and
# fails this case. Same geometry as lonpole_tan_lp150.
NOTE pipeline: zenithal TAN with explicit non-default LONPOLE = 0
GRID -100 612 9 -100 612 9
PIX 256.5 256.5
SKY 250 15
SKYGRID 245 255 5 35 45 5
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 512
NAXIS2  = 512
CTYPE1  = 'RA---TAN'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--TAN'
CRVAL1  = 250.0
CRVAL2  = 40.0
CRPIX1  = 256.5
CRPIX2  = 256.5
CDELT1  = -0.01
CDELT2  = 0.01
LONPOLE = 0.0
